# Private terms — NOT committed to the repository.
#
# One term per line, case-insensitive, matched as a substring anywhere in
# src/, public/, scripts/, README.md, ANONYMIZATION.md and the built HTML.
# Lines starting with # are ignored.
#
# This file is git-ignored on purpose: a denylist committed to the tree would
# itself publish the names it is meant to protect. Keep the mechanism in the
# repository, keep the list on the machine.
#
# Placeholder entries below are examples of the *shape* to add. Replace them
# with the real names, brands, hostnames and identifiers that must never be
# published.

EXAMPLE-client-name
EXAMPLE-brand
EXAMPLE-project-codename
EXAMPLE-firstname
EXAMPLE-surname
EXAMPLE-username
